[
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's a syntax rule for a pair of identifiers:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Suppose that I want a parser that produces a <code>pair</code> only when the identifier names together satisfy some property.   For example, let's say that they should have the same first letter.  If that property is not met, the parser should fail and consume nothing.</p>\n<p>After reading the code in <code>Lean/Parser/Basic.lean</code> and thinking about it for a while, I came up with this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match_fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ParserFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stxStack</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extract</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stack</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">front</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">front</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkUnexpectedError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"expected match\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkUnexpectedError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"idents expected\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epsilonInfo</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match_fn</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">combinator_formatter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkStackTopEnv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">formatter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Formatter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">combinator_parenthesizer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkStackTopEnv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parenthesizer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parenthesizer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matching_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It seems to work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">matching_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$_</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Macro</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baz</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeeds</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces 5</span>\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">yo</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>My question for the macro gurus is simply this: is this the easiest way?  Or is there some combinator or technique that would let me write this more easily?</p>",
        "id": 630621769,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1791631850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK, I thought about it a bit more and found an easier way:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mk_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">front</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toString</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">front</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matching_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">atomic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mk_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkStackTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"expected match\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I certainly like this better.</p>",
        "id": 630622766,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1791632692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>However, it's still a bit annoying that I have to write <code>mk_pair</code>.  I wanted to write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matching_pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">atomic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pair</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checkStackTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">check_match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"expected match\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However that won't compile, because <code>pair</code> is a <code>ParserDescr</code>, not a <code>Parser</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthesize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">HAndThen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ParserDescr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">3</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is <code>mk_pair</code> simply necessary here, or can I avoid it somehow?</p>",
        "id": 630623044,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1791632912
    }
